sequenceDiagram
    actor Customer as PER-001 (Customer)
    participant Channel as SVC-017<br/>Digital Channels
    participant IAM as SVC-100<br/>IAM
    participant DomPay as SVC-009<br/>Domestic Payments
    participant Retail as SVC-001<br/>Retail Banking Core
    participant Audit as SVC-103<br/>Audit & Logging

    Note over Customer,Audit: PY-001 — Payment Initiation (insufficient funds detected synchronously)
    Note right of Customer: Account available balance: £120.50<br/>Payment amount requested: £500.00

    Customer->>Channel: Enter payee details, amount: £500.00
    Channel->>DomPay: POST /cop/verify {payee_sort_code, payee_account_number, payee_name}
    DomPay-->>Channel: 200 OK {cop_result: match, risk_warning_required: false}
    Channel-->>Customer: CoP result: "Payee verified ✓" — prompt SCA

    Customer->>Channel: Complete SCA (biometric)
    Channel->>IAM: POST /sca/validate {assertion, payee_sort_code, payee_account_number, amount: 500.00}
    IAM-->>Channel: 200 OK {sca_assertion_ref, valid: true}

    Channel->>Retail: POST /payments {account_id, amount: 500.00, payee details, cop_result: match, sca_assertion_ref}

    Note right of Retail: Validate account: active ✓<br/>Check balance: £120.50 < £500.00 ✗<br/>FAIL — no PaymentIntent created<br/>No events published

    Retail->>Audit: Log rejected payment attempt (account_id, amount, reason: insufficient_funds)
    Note right of Audit: Operational log only — not WORM pipeline<br/>(no financial transaction occurred)

    Retail-->>Channel: 402 Payment Required<br/>{error_code: INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS,<br/>available_balance: "120.50"}

    Channel-->>Customer: "Insufficient funds. Your available balance is £120.50.<br/>The payment has not been processed.<br/>Please reduce the amount or top up your account."

    Note over Customer,Audit: Journey terminates here — synchronous rejection<br/>No screening, no fraud check, no events published<br/>Customer shown specific, actionable message (FCA Consumer Duty)
